│  │ SLAVE ESP32                                      │       │
│  │ ┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │       │
│  │ │ • Parses commands from master              │  │       │
│  │ │ • Reads sensors (IMU, encoder, GPS)        │  │       │
│  │ │ • Computes robot odometry/pose             │  │       │
│  │ │ • Sends status packets to master           │  │       │
│  │ └────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │       │
│  │         │                                         │       │
│  │         │ UART1 (GPIO18 TX, GPIO19 RX)          │       │
│  │         │ 115200 baud                           │       │
│  │         ↓                                         │       │
│  │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐       │       │
│  │  │ ARDUINO MEGA                         │       │       │
│  │  │ • Motor control (drive)              │       │       │
│  │  │ • Servo control (arm joints)         │       │       │
│  │  │ • Gripper control                    │       │       │
│  │  │ • Receives commands: "B90 S45..."    │       │       │
│  │  │ • Receives commands: "PICK..."       │       │       │
│  │  └──────────────────────────────────────┘       │       │
│  │         │                                         │       │
│  │         ├─→ PWM to motor drivers                 │       │
│  │         ├─→ PWM to servo motors                  │       │
│  │         └─→ Digital/analog to actuators          │       │
│  │                                                   │       │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘       │
│                                                               │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


🔌 Connection Details:
Master ESP32 ↔ Slave ESP32 (UART2)
text
Master GPIO17 (TX) → Slave GPIO16 (RX)
Master GPIO16 (RX) ← Slave GPIO17 (TX)
GND → GND (common ground)


Slave ESP32 ↔ Arduino Mega (UART1)
text
Slave GPIO18 (TX) → Arduino Mega RX0 (or RX1, RX2, RX3)
Slave GPIO19 (RX) ← Arduino Mega TX0 (or TX1, TX2, TX3)
GND → GND (common ground)

📊 Data Flow:
User opens web UI on master ESP32 (browser → master)

User clicks "Send Joint Angles" with values B90 S45 E135 W90

Master sends text command to slave via UART2: "B90 S45 E135 W90\n"

Slave receives command, parses it

Slave forwards to Arduino Mega via UART1: "B90 S45 E135 W90\n"

Arduino Mega reads command, controls servos to those angles

Slave reads sensors (IMU, encoder, ultrasonic)

Slave sends status packet back to master every 200ms

Master updates web UI with robot position and obstacles

⚙️ Why This Architecture?
Master ESP32: High-level control, web UI, Wi-Fi communication (less real-time critical)

Slave ESP32: Mid-level, sensor fusion, command routing, timing-sensitive (better for real-time)

Arduino Mega: Low-level hardware control, motor/servo PWM (best for real-time precision)

